DESCRIPTION:Veterans Day falls on November 11 and honors everyone who serve
 d honorably in the United States armed forces\, in wartime or peacetime\, 
 living or dead. The date is not symbolic: it is the hour the guns stopped 
 in the First World War\, 11 a.m. on November 11\, 1918. For its first 36 y
 ears the holiday was called Armistice Day\, and for seven years in the 197
 0s it was not observed on November 11 at all.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.c
 om/holiday/veterans-day/
